# sw001, the salt-weigher (test fixture): written for the talk town's Saltwell storekeeper.
mantle sw001
state ready
dialect saltwell
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for tt_sa_storekeeper
title the salt-weigher
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=merchant
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=dry
quirk weighs_everything_twice
likes well_water
dislikes short_weight
fears a_dry_well
hopes a_good_season
topics prices +.3 times +.2
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# keeps the stores by the pans: dry, careful, and weighs everything twice.

words
saying! = Salt keeps, and so do debts | Weigh twice, sell once
oath! = By the pans | Salt and sun
greet = Peace on your step | Sun and shade to you

rule @scales
when concept=bark working=yes self.role=merchant
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Weighed twice and fair. Salt, oil, rope. | Short weight's a sin under the sun. Not at my scales.

scene weighing
when concept=talk.prices
does tell.complaint / react.complaint
a : I weighed the last sack twice and it still came up short. Somebody's thumb is on the scale up the road.
b : There's always a thumb on it somewhere.

line greet.return : #greet#. Mind the salt on the step.
line farewell.return : #farewell#.
line react.news.new : #oath#! And on a day like this.
line react.news.known : I'd heard it at the well.
line answer.how : Weighed and found fair, mostly.
line preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. The scales won't watch themselves.

dlg shop.greet [here.shop!=bare] : #greet#. Salt, oil, rope, all weighed twice.
